From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: Derive every YUV stream from one full size capture stream

The software ISP crops instead of scaling: a 640x480 stream of its own is the
centre of the sensor picture, a zoom of 2.5. It also writes with a stride
equal to the width, which is not what gralloc gives for most sizes.

- configureStreams() asks the camera for a single NV12 stream, at the size of
  the JPEG stream if there is one and at the largest supported size
  otherwise, captured into buffers of the HAL. All Android YUV streams are
  Mapped streams; without JPEG stream the first of them stands for the
  source.
- The YUV post-processor scales the centre crop of the source that has the
  aspect ratio of the destination (16:9 from a 4:3 sensor was stretched),
  with the strides of the destination buffer.
- The generic CameraBuffer takes the plane layout from minigbm buffer
  handles (msm: stride aligned to 128, Y lines to 32).
---
--- a/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
@@ -485,6 +485,22 @@
  * stream configurations to be reported to the Android camera framework through
  * the camera static metadata.
  */
+Size CameraCapabilities::maxYuvSize() const
+{
+	Size maxSize;
+
+	for (const Camera3StreamConfiguration &entry : streamConfigurations_) {
+		if (entry.androidFormat != HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_YCbCr_420_888)
+			continue;
+
+		if (entry.resolution.width * entry.resolution.height >
+		    maxSize.width * maxSize.height)
+			maxSize = entry.resolution;
+	}
+
+	return maxSize;
+}
